    "chapters": [
      {
        "id": "models",
        "title": "Mixtral configuration, assembly and inherited execution paths",
        "claims": [
          {
            "text": "Adding MixtralModel to the registry comprehension exposes MixtralForCausalLM with its configuration and model classes. The new configuration requires intermediate_size, num_local_experts and num_experts_per_tok, mapping them to the existing routed-MLP constructor. Parent searches distinguish these from Qwen3 MoE\u2019s moe_intermediate_size and num_experts spellings.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_aac1f07bff33408d9495d73e53f0ab19",
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27",
              "call_af2ba0dd32d540e7865978653b550ea9",
              "call_fb3459e5345d46748611a755e860f6ec",
              "call_d4cda7493e834fb9a52c6619f10007a8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Explicit head_dim is retained; otherwise it is hidden_size divided by query-head count using integer division. KV-head count defaults to query-head count, tied embeddings default to false, and a supplied hidden_act must be silu. RoPE uses the existing default-settings reader with NEOX style.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27",
              "call_f946dbb3ae50497ab402e25421fd0890"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The builder closely follows Qwen3MoeModel, but omits its Q/K normalization, changes the MLP prefix to block_sparse_moe, maps gate/up/down to w1/w3/w2, and requests half rather than float MLP output. It also omits Qwen3MoeModel\u2019s calibration_all_experts=True assignment.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27",
              "call_50119befce924239b024a4c2bd79e78f"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Each layer applies input RMSNorm, attention and a residual addition, followed by post-attention RMSNorm, routed MLP and another residual addition. Attention uses q_proj/k_proj/v_proj/o_proj, no Q/K norms, no sliding window override and sm_scale=None. Its existing implementations handle uncached SDPA, uncached FlashAttention and cached FlashAttention; this patch supplies no new backend.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27",
              "call_0febcec3f60643ffbdc02b9006bca2d8",
              "call_f2429752a1c84585bf0736d259f4184b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "BlockSparseMLP projects router scores, applies softmax, selects top experts and renormalizes their weights. Each selected expert computes down(SiLU(w1(x)) \u00d7 w3(x)); weighted outputs are accumulated into token order. The routing projection uses pad_to=1, preserving exactly the expert count, while expert projections retain Linear\u2019s default 128-element alignment.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27",
              "call_78fbdc61ce8747edb0718c48dc8bc502",
              "call_e554464f43d346b287afd441a248c5b8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The existing grouped-expert path handles multiple flattened tokens or non-EXL3 experts. One flattened token with every expert projection in EXL3 selects indexed multi-GEMMs. MultiLinear additionally requires matching dimensions and bit widths within each projection group, no biases or softcaps, and unit post-scaling. The new Mixtral caller inherits these restrictions.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_78fbdc61ce8747edb0718c48dc8bc502",
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "The only pre-existing BlockSparseMLP model construction found is Qwen3 MoE. Its all-expert calibration override ensures every down projection is visited during capture. Mixtral instead inherits Model\u2019s false default: conversion supplies that value to activate_all_experts, leaving capture sparse. Gate/up projections share block.mlp.input; each down projection has its own block.mlp.{expert}.down capture key.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_3405f7921fee4410bbe054c0c120bc15",
              "call_50119befce924239b024a4c2bd79e78f",
              "call_70c9c088207f436f823c98992deedb1a",
              "call_3b8a7cfe24864bc1bb01863f2d45d2fb",
              "call_78fbdc61ce8747edb0718c48dc8bc502"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Assembly ends with model.norm and lm_head. Tying enables model.embed_tokens as an alternate head key; Linear still tries supported storage at its primary key first. prepare_inputs stores input_ids and delegates to prepare_for_attn, whose default is uncached FlashAttention and whose uncached preparation rejects a supplied cache.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27",
              "call_e554464f43d346b287afd441a248c5b8",
              "call_f2429752a1c84585bf0736d259f4184b"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "mistralai/Mixtral-8x7B-v0.1 and Mixtral-8x7B-Instruct-v0.1 each match the registration and configuration mappings: hidden size 4096, intermediate size 14336, 32 layers, 32 query heads, eight KV heads, eight experts with two selected, vocabulary 32000 and maximum positions 32768. Both specify SiLU, RMS epsilon 1e-5, RoPE theta 1000000, untied embeddings and no sliding window.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_cb8e3fc1f20b4b87a813b30a834cc8b1",
              "call_4eec33d549e94a248a2ce0955c110ab8",
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "mistralai/Mixtral-8x22B-v0.1 and Mixtral-8x22B-Instruct-v0.1 each match the mappings with hidden size 6144, intermediate size 16384, 56 layers, 48 query heads, eight KV heads, eight experts with two selected and maximum positions 65536. Their vocabularies differ: 32000 for base and 32768 for Instruct. Both retain SiLU, epsilon 1e-5, theta 1000000, untied embeddings and no sliding window.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_50dba8bd77f645c6a42d513f3408a91a",
              "call_f70a0f57696445ada081df73ff943232",
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Sampled checkpoint headers agree with the requested weight families and orientation: w1/w3 are [intermediate, hidden], w2 is [hidden, intermediate], router weights are [8, hidden], Q/O are [hidden, hidden], K/V are [1024, hidden], norms are [hidden], and embeddings/head are [vocabulary, hidden]. These stored matrices are transposed by Linear.load_fp16. Sampled headers contain no optional biases or EXL3 scale/su/suh/sv/svh/trellis tensors, so the ordinary weight-loading path applies to these samples; tying is disabled in all four configurations. Every tensor in the inspected shards belongs to a requested weight family; no unused stored tensor was identified there.",
            "basis": "source",
            "evidence": [
              "call_be406182c92c4a389522fdc03aa7a99f",
              "call_d25236324f7f4558a6d5efe892b5ce73",
              "call_d3c1677783e54b26bb21731358d9948d",
              "call_10a80c9daa984b3f88ecc9d71033a3f4",
              "call_19327663a96040ab8b282f080ca76e6c",
              "call_956b0e39744b4ad19b6dbe89d1243edb",
              "call_e554464f43d346b287afd441a248c5b8"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Standard-library arithmetic gives head dimension 128 and KV width 1024 for all inspected configurations. Query widths are 4096 and 6144, with four or six query heads per KV head. Hidden, intermediate and vocabulary dimensions are divisible by 128, so default alignment adds no padding. Selecting two of eight experts is 25% of the expert set, not a measured fraction of total computation.",
            "basis": "execution",
            "evidence": [
              "call_5708122539954b908a4fe826ebd2d6fd"
            ]
          },
          {
            "text": "Reusing shared modules reduces architecture-specific implementation work, but also imports their calibration requirements and fused-path restrictions. The two edits are complementary: registration exposes the new builder, while the builder supplies the checkpoint-specific names and dimensions needed by that dispatch.",
            "basis": "inference",
            "evidence": [
              "call_aac1f07bff33408d9495d73e53f0ab19",
              "call_d5131c10b83a48a1b38611bbe396bc27",
              "call_78fbdc61ce8747edb0718c48dc8bc502"
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "mixtral-sparse-calibration-coverage",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "Mixtral omits the existing all-expert calibration override, allowing expert-specific capture data to be missing during conversion.",
        "trigger": "A Mixtral layer\u2019s calibration tokens never select at least one expert, while conversion subsequently attempts to quantize all its expert projections.",
        "expected_behavior": "Collect calibration input for every down projection, or handle an unvisited expert explicitly.",
        "actual_behavior": "Model defaults calibration_all_experts to false. BlockSparseMLP skips unselected experts, and Linear creates capture entries only when forwarded. Conversion later indexes capture_H[linear.qmap] for every loaded quantization target, so an unvisited down projection has no entry and the lookup raises KeyError. The inspected Qwen3 MoE construction prevents this coverage gap with its true override. Direct convert_exl3 callers found were conversion main and test_quant_dequant; the test explicitly forwards its individual Linear before conversion and does not exercise routed coverage.",
        "locations": [
          {
            "commit": "9665ba99989955593d2fb148323c9a96c77d1bea",
            "path": "exllamav3/models/mixtral.py",
