      {
        "id": "inherited-all-expert-fused-dimensions",
        "origin": "authoring_observation",
        "status": "suspected",
        "classification": "defect",
        "description": "The previously recorded all-expert fused-buffer mismatch remains unchanged in the implementation newly used by Mixtral.",
        "trigger": "Forward one flattened token through fully EXL3 Mixtral experts with activate_all_experts=True.",
        "expected_behavior": "Evaluate all eight experts with suitably sized buffers or use the grouped-expert path.",
        "actual_behavior": "Routing produces eight indices, but fused buffers retain num_experts_per_tok=2 slots. The first exl3_mgemm checks index count against the output expert dimension and rejects the mismatch. Model.forward passes caller parameters through TransformerBlock to its MLP, establishing conditional API reach. Parent search also found ParallelDecoderBlock forwarding parameters, but Mixtral uses TransformerBlock. Ordinary Mixtral conversion supplies false and does not establish this trigger.",
